#
# Seed the pacman *installed* (local) db on first boot so archr-update /
# `pacman -Syu` can upgrade the BASE system, not just user-installed addons.
#
# The image rootfs is not a pacman install, so /var/lib/pacman
# (-> /storage/.pacman/db) starts empty: `pacman -Q` returns nothing and
# `pacman -Qu` finds no upgrades even when the repo carries newer base
# packages. archr-update seeds it from the db the image build recorded of
# its own packages, so no network is needed and the versions are the ones
# this rootfs really has. It does nothing once the db holds entries (seeded
# earlier, or by the user's own pacman activity).

mkdir -p /storage/.pacman/db
/usr/bin/archr-update seed >>/var/log/pacman-seed.log 2>&1 || :
